 g that takes place in\, or is focused on\, the city of Atlanta. 2026 RESEA
 RCH AREAS: Data Centers\; AI Civics\; AI Literacies\; AI and Archives\; Sm
 all Language Models\; Capitalism\, Anticapitalism\, and Critique. WHO: fac
 ulty\, staff (including library staff)\, graduate students and members of 
 Atlanta-based community organizations.\n\nOrganisation: Atlanta Interdisci
 plinary AI Network (AIAI)\, Mellon Foundation funded\nLocation: Atlanta\, 
 Georgia\, USA. Projects must take place in or focus on Atlanta\; every tea
 m needs at least one Atlanta-based researcher.\nAward: Up to USD 5\,000 pe
 r project. In line with Mellon policy\, no institutional overhead may be c
 harged. Individuals taking the award outside an institution or employer pa
 y income tax on it. No application fee.\nDuration: Funds distributed early
  January 2027\; must be spent by 1 August 2027 (about 7 months).\n\nMore: 
 https://www.aiai.network/grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
