 prints 2027-28 (cross-border theatre and digital artist teams)
DESCRIPTION:ETC's Digital Theatre Programme pairs two member theatres from 
 different countries with a Digital Expert to research and develop artistic
  uses of technology in theatre: motion capture\, coding\, mixed\, augmente
 d and virtual reality\, robotics and interaction design. The work runs as 
 a development sprint and a research sprint\, with time at the Akademie fü
 r Theater und Digitalität in Dortmund.\n\nOrganisation: European Theatre 
 Convention (ETC) with the Akademie für Theater und Digitalität\, Dortmun
 d\nLocation: Europe. Joint applications from two ETC member theatres in di
 fferent countries\; the Digital Expert works in residence with them.\nAwar
 d: EUR 3\,000 development grant shared between the two partner theatres\, 
 plus up to EUR 2\,860 from ETC for the Digital Expert's travel\, accommoda
 tion and subsistence. The theatres must put the Digital Expert on their pa
 yroll at their usual creative fee. No application fee.\nDuration: Two spri
 nts of up to 42 days of residency in total: Path A runs a spring 2027 deve
 lopment sprint and an autumn 2027 research sprint\; Path B runs autumn 202
 7 and spring 2028. Academy visit in March 2027.\n\nMore: https://europeant
 heatre.eu/events/etcs-digital-theatre-programme-research-development-sprin
 ts-10?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
